# In a loop the left element of a sum of two elements reads a hole as NaN only where the right side is no text: it comes off a list of numbers tested in front of the loop. Here both lists are parameters, so nothing but a written
# key stands between the two reads, and the right one holds texts: the left element keeps its hole: past the end it gives undefined, and the sum is "undefinedx". One read alone reads its hole as NaN: the one under the product.
# What the safeguard is worth is asked by a lie in the file beside this one.
